# ---- OS / editor ---------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Vendored Microsoft interop assemblies. Committed deliberately so the build is hermetic -- see
# lib/README.md. Without this negation the *.dll rule above silently excludes them and a fresh clone
# cannot compile, which is exactly the failure vendoring was meant to prevent.
!lib/*.dll

# ---- AI tooling, machine-local -------------------------------------------
# The AI Token Optimizer extension rewrites these whenever the workspace opens, and they carry
# per-machine settings. AGENTS.md is the committed contract, and .github/copilot-instructions.md
# is tracked because GitHub reads it server-side; both are generic and reviewed before landing.
CLAUDE.md
.codex/
.cavemanrc
.aicache/
.codegraph/
